  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8f9160b2-f2ec-4463-b066-aeb1fe2ed28c-image.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 259px;\" />Methoxy group increases the pKa of the phenol group - it makes it less acidic. The oxygen atom does indeed exert an electron-withdrawing inductive effect, but the lone pairs on the oxygen cause the exact opposite effect So the methoxy group is an electron-donating group by resonance.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e64b9a3a-a36e-47e3-aa42-57a21d05404a-image.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 309px;\" /></p>",
